---------- Forwarded message ----------

Check out http://www.tisya.co.in/indy/

26th January, 2002 - Announcing Indy, version 0.1, Alpha release.

We wish to announce the alpha release of Indy Operating Environment for the 
Linux kernel.

Indy OE has its beginings in a vision to provide the world with a 
combination of, power offered by the Linux kernel and a minimalist yet, an 
elegant and easy to use interface.

Though the project has been a personal research effort for the past four 
years, most of the coding has been done in the past 26 days only.

With this release, we invite you to test out the first two applications 
from us and send us feedback about them.
Please send feedback to feedback at tisya dot co dot in
Please click here to download.

To see screenshots, click here.

Instructions for installing and using IndyOE.

Pre-requisites
nAn already running Linux installation (we will release an independent 
distro soon).
nCapability to run as root user
nLinux kernel supporting the graphics framebuffer
nA working graphics framebuffer running in 16 bit mode at atleast 640x480 
resolution
(you should see the Tux logo while booting
nWillingness to try out alpha software ;^)

Installation and usage
Download the software (from here)
Copy the file (indy.tgz) to your top level directory (/).
Change over to that directory by issuing cd /
Expand the file by issuing tar -xzvf indy.tgz
Run it by issuing . ./runoe

MP3 PlayerMailerAll
Standard disclaimer
This software is alpha level, though it has been tested out on our system 
and hasn't caused any damage till date, we refrain from assuming 
responsibility for any damage caused to your system or any losses incurred 
by you thereof.


