tsprof generates a subroutine call execution profile, without recompiling
and without relinking.  tsprof presents the measurements using colorful
interactive and print graphics, with tabular text available.  If you
can run your application, then tsprof shows you where your code spends
its time, and helps you understand and tune its performance.

tsprof works with main programs, shared libraries, dynamic loaded modules,
pthreads, and SMP; all with no recompiling and no relinking.  tsprof
measures time directly, with cycle-by-cycle precision.  For serious
performance analysis, pmprof works the same way but also covers
processor events such as cache misses, pipeline stalls, etc.

Get tsprof and pmprof today for i586+ machines running Linux.
For sample output and more information, visit http://www.BitWagon.com .


BitWagon Software LLC

