mkshrc produces variants of Bourne-shell and C-shell scripts from a
single source file. It is intended to be used by system administrators
who want to provide consistent initialization files for different
shells.

mkshrc is distributed under the terms of the GNU General Public
License. It has be developped under Linux but should work on any UNIX
system.

Feature list:
=============
- Produce several variants: sh, csh, bash, ksh, tcsh.
- Full support for flow control (for, while, switch, if-else)
- Support for aliases with arguments restricted to C-shell
  functionalities (implemented with functions in Bourne-like shells).
- Support for conditional expressions
- Support for variable assignments
- Full documentation included
- Test suite included

Download location:
==================
http://home.earthlink.net/~lpelecq/mkshrc/index.en.html

If this URL is broken in the future, use the permanent URL below and
follow links.
  http://www.soleil.org/laurent.pelecq

--
Laurent Pelecq

